    {
      "id": "tide-sig-06",
      "name": "Corvath signature",
      "shortName": "Discard Void Depth",
      "summary": "A discard-driven tide that builds void depth as a resource, rewarding it with void-presence power boosts and massive void-banishing finishers, distinguishing itself from the Vrakmoth signature's abandon-sacrifice engines by treating discard as its primary fuel rather than sacrificing characters.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-06 is a heavily character-weighted deck (84 of 110 copies are characters) built around the loop of aggressive discarding to fill the void and then cashing in that depth for escalating power. The discard engine runs through multiple double-copies: Sunken Radiance draws two and discards two while recovering energy, Evacuation Enforcer and Grotto Seer / Urban Cipher wholesale replace the hand, and Wasteland Arbitrator symmetrically discards on entry while recurring for cheap. That churning void unlocks the tide's payoff layer — Soulkindler passively grants all allied characters +1✦ simply by sitting in the void, Paradox Enforcer is a 7-spark unstoppable attacker that banishes seven void cards to materialize, Vessel of Echoes jumps to +5✦ when six or more cards accumulate there, and Weight of Memory dissolves any enemy whose spark is at most the void count. A parallel Awakened anthem (Pyrestone Avatar and Pinnacle Ascendant both appear at 2x) activates ally ☪ abilities the moment they hit play, amplifying every draw-discard loop card on the board. A secondary survivor token cluster (Dustborn Veteran, Defiant Holdout, Shadowcaller, Sorrow Watcher) gives the tide a resilient ground presence as the void fills. Compared to the nearest sibling tide-fac-32, which uses the same discard package as a tight 45-card splash without the survivor token sub-theme or the high-cost void finishers, this signature tide goes much deeper on void accumulation payoffs. Against tide-sig-04 (Vrakmoth), both tides share erode and discard cycling, but Vrakmoth converts characters into fuel via abandon-for-energy and abandon-for-removal engines (Kindlehorn, Shadowbinder, Stolen Genesis), while tide-sig-06 keeps its characters on board and mines value from the growing void itself.",
      "role": "signature",
