    {
      "id": "tide-sig-07",
      "name": "Kael Voss signature",
      "shortName": "Survivor Token Reclaim",
      "summary": "A survivor-tribal engine that continuously replaces dissolved non-figments with survivor figments, draws cards off the growing board, and loops key pieces from the void to threaten an unstoppable finisher — distinguishing itself from the nearest sibling (Vaela) by building board mass and void depth rather than converting each sacrifice into immediate energy or spark.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-07 is a character-dense survivor tribal deck with 92 characters and 18 events, built around a self-replenishing token board and a deepening void that pays off over a long game. The core engine runs through a cluster of 2x survivors: Dustborn Veteran converts every dissolved non-figment survivor into a 1✦ survivor figment, Sorrow Watcher churns out additional figments at will and draws a card for each group of three allied survivors, and Tidewreck Navigator exchanges discarded cards for figments or retrieves survivors straight from the void. These pieces together mean dissolving a survivor rarely loses the board — it typically replaces itself and often replaces itself with a card. The void loop is reinforced by Ashwalker (erodes on materialization, returns a character from the void when dissolved), Graywatch (returns itself to play whenever you play any card from the void), Veil of the Wastes (returns itself from the void each time you materialize a cheap character), and Duskwall Delver (reclaims itself for 1● whenever any ally is dissolved), creating a persistent stream of bodies that feeds both the Sorrow Watcher draw trigger and Paradox Enforcer's endgame condition — that 7✦ unstoppable character costs only 1● once seven cards have accumulated in the void. Where the nearest sibling Vaela (tide-sig-08) prioritizes converting each individual abandon into an immediate reward (energy from Nightmare Manifest, ✦ growth on Cinderheart, ⍟ from Skull Weaver), sig-07 invests sacrifices into board replenishment and void accumulation, trading burst resource generation for a resilient, self-sustaining army that builds inevitably toward a void-powered win condition.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
