    {
      "id": "tide-sig-08",
      "name": "Vaela signature",
      "shortName": "Abandon Energy Engine",
      "summary": "Tide-sig-08 is an abandon-for-energy engine that cycles low-cost survivors as fuel to generate ●, replace dissolved characters with figments, and recur threats from the void — distinguishing itself from its nearest sibling (tide-sig-07) by centering energy accumulation over discard synergies, and from tide-sig-02 by prioritizing survivor resilience and void recursion over draw payoffs from dissolution.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-08 is built almost entirely on Characters (89 of 110 copies), with a dense cluster of inexpensive survivors that serve as both board presence and sacrifice fuel. The central engine runs through abandonment: Nightmare Manifest (☪, Abandon a character: Gain 1●) and Exiles of the Last Light (Abandon another character: Gain 1●) convert each sacrificed ally directly into energy, while Volcanic Channeler and Entropy Spike extend that loop by generating ● or maximum-● whenever any ally is dissolved. Abandoning characters feeds payoff pieces simultaneously — Cinderheart grows +1✦ per abandon and converts that ✦ into ⍟ on dissolution, Harvester of Despair similarly stacks +1✦ each time you sacrifice another character, and Skull Weaver and Fathomless Maw drain ⍟ whenever allies leave play. The dissolution-replacement package maintains board presence under this attrition: Dustborn Veteran materializes a 1✦ survivor figment whenever a non-figment survivor is dissolved, Shadowcaller does the same for any ally, and Sorrow Watcher can produce figments directly with a ☪ activation. Energy built by the sacrifice loop then pays for a deep void-recursion suite — Duskwall Delver re-enters play for 1● whenever an ally dissolves, Veil of the Wastes returns from your void every time you materialize a ≤2● character, and Graywatch returns to play each time you play any card from your void — which together keep the board populated and create the fuel for unstoppable late-game threats like The Rising God (Reclaim – 2●, Abandon two characters, Unstoppable). Compared to tide-sig-07 (Kael Voss), which shares several survivor staples but extends into dedicated discard-payoff cards such as Torchbearer of the Abyss, Gleamharvester, and Marrow Drinker, this tide stays focused on the energy-from-abandonment axis and runs its discard package only as removal enablement (Maelstrom Denial, Pyrokinetic Surge). Compared to tide-sig-02 (Caedryn), which runs Soulreaver and Scuttled Fortune at double copies to convert dissolution into draw, and uses Stolen Genesis and Apocalypse as its big payoffs, this tide converts dissolution into energy and void recursion rather than card advantage, making its loop more self-sustaining and less reliant on burst draw to close games.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
