    {
      "id": "tide-sig-09",
      "name": "Edran signature",
      "shortName": "Event Copy Engine",
      "summary": "A heavy-event control tide that wins by copying and recycling events — building explosive chained turns through copy-on-play enchantments and void-event-as-resource payoffs — where its nearest sibling (tide-sig-10) shares the countermagic skeleton but instead pursues clean filtering, mass hand resets, and tutor tools with no copying engine whatsoever.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-09 is a deeply event-heavy tide (62 events, 48 characters) built around a two-layered engine: first, establishing characters that reward playing events — Duskshore Virtuoso accumulates ⧗ counters per event played and cashes them for +5✦, The Ringleader creates an ephemeral copy of the next event on materialization, and Echo Architect copies every event played at the cost of 1● extra per event — and second, recycling key events from the void through Minstrel of Falling Light, Archive of the Forgotten, From the Barrow, and Spirit of Smoldering Echoes, with Architect of Memory threatening +4✦ and awakened whenever three or more events sit in the graveyard. The countermagic backbone — Defiant Parry, Abolish, Echoing Denial, Crumbling Covenant, Ripple Through Reality — keeps opponents off key plays while the engine assembles, and Ridgecutter's bounce-plus-ramp doubles as tempo disruption and energy acceleration. Big turns are enabled by Cascade of Reflections (copy every event until end of turn), Cascading Detonation (copy the next event twice with a reclaim stapled on), and Echoes of the Journey (draw an ephemeral free card for each card already played). Compared to tide-sig-10, which runs the same countermagic package but pivots toward deck filtering (multiple Sunset Chapel Rest, Gleam Below, Ecliptic Vantage), mass hand resets (Wheel of the Heavens, Starfall Communion), and tutor tools (Rite of Summoning, Door to Possibility), tide-sig-09 is defined entirely by copy multiplication and void recursion: it wants events to pile up in the graveyard as fuel and then chain copies of them in a single explosive turn rather than sculpting a perfect hand over multiple turns.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
