    {
      "id": "tide-sig-10",
      "name": "Zeva signature",
      "shortName": "Event Chain Combo",
      "summary": "A heavy event-centric tide that wins by copying and chaining events in a single turn, supported by void reclaim to replay key pieces — where its nearest sibling (tide-sig-09) grinds through discard cycling and character-based void payoffs, this tide builds toward explosive multi-event turns that score directly or reset the board.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-10 is a high-event deck (69 events, 41 characters) built around a central combo engine: play multiple events in one turn, copy them, and cash out the chain for score or decisive board control. The copying payoffs are layered across the pool — Echo Architect makes each event cost 1 more but creates a free copy whenever one resolves; The Ringleader creates an ephemeral copy of the next event you play; Cascade of Reflections copies every event until end of turn; Cascading Detonation copies the next event twice and reclaims itself; and Broadcast Array cashes the whole chain directly into score, uncounterable. To fuel these chains, the tide includes aggressive void reclaim: Dreadwood Emissary gives a void event reclaim on materialization, Spirit of Smoldering Echoes pays 2 energy to reclaim a void event, Archive of the Forgotten reclaims up to two events at once, and From the Barrow grants mass reclaim for a full turn. The interrupt-heavy backbone — Defiant Parry, Ridgecutter, Fractured Veil, Abolish, Crumbling Covenant — keeps opponents off balance while the player assembles their chain. Compared to tide-sig-09, which generates card velocity through discard loops (Pattern Seeker, Key Sifter, Call of Calamity, Minstrel of Falling Light) and leans on character-synergy payoffs in the void (Soulkindler, Pinnacle Ascendant), tide-sig-10 invests that same draw density into setting up a single explosive turn where copied events chain into a winning score burst.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
