    {
      "id": "tide-sig-14",
      "name": "Yveth Coravel signature",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Ramp",
      "summary": "A spirit animal energy-ramp tide that builds wide boards of cheap Dawn-trigger creatures to fuel burst finishers, distinguished from its sibling tides by a banish-heavy removal suite and warrior sub-synergies rather than cost-reduction engines or reclaim recursion.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-14 is built almost entirely on Characters (93 of 110 copies), with a dense package of 1-cost spirit animals — Ethereal Trailblazer, Blazebound Sentinel, Worldsong Behemoth, Undying Fang, and others — that each generate 1● on Dawn, creating a self-accelerating energy engine the wider the board grows. Mid-range payoffs like Skyborne Jellyfish (\"Gain 1● for each allied ≤2● cost character\"), Blazing Emberwing (\"Gain 1● for each allied character\"), Ghostlight Wolves (\"Gain 1● for each allied spirit animal\"), and Mountainwatch Alpha reinforce this ramp, while Moonbound Wolf lets you replay Dawn triggers on demand and Stoneborn Eternal bounces itself free whenever another spirit animal is played. The accumulated energy drives finishers: Spiritbound Alpha gives the whole pack +3✦ and vengeful for 5●, Spirit Bond scales every ally's ✦ by board count and makes them unstoppable, and Mystic Runefish can set every spirit animal's ✦ to 7 in one activation. Where nearest sibling tide-sig-15 reaches for Nexus Wayfinder at 2x (making all ≤2● characters free) and Abomination of Memory as a void-threshold payoff, and tide-sig-17 leans on Starrunner at 2x plus bounce and reclaim tools for recursive value, tide-sig-14 instead runs a banish-based removal layer — fast interrupt Bladefall, Shattering Gambit, Ambush Operative on entry, and the challenge-step Gatebound Warden — alongside warrior sub-synergies (Assault Leader, Eclipse Herald's stored-⧗ dissolve, Shadow Reflection) that give the deck interactive tempo tools its siblings lack.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
