    {
      "id": "tide-sig-16",
      "name": "Radulf signature",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Swarm Sculpt",
      "summary": "Builds a wide board of cheap spirit animals to ramp energy through Dawn triggers, then wins with either a massed burst finisher or a concentrated single-attacker strike, distinguished from its nearest siblings by doubled-up hand-sculpting tools and a lone-challenger payoff rather than mass Dawn re-triggering engines.",
      "description": "This tide is overwhelmingly character-heavy (93 of 110 copies), anchored in cheap spirit animals that generate energy at Dawn — cards like Ethereal Trailblazer, Undying Fang, Blazebound Sentinel, and Worldsong Behemoth each trigger \"gain 1●\" every Dawn, while Skyborne Jellyfish scales that yield with the number of allied ≤2● cost characters in play. Nexus Wayfinder (making all ≤2● characters free) and the recurring bounce of Stoneborn Eternal let the deck flood the board before pivoting to finishers: Spirit Bond grants unstoppable and +X✦ equal to your ally count, Spiritbound Alpha gives spirit animals +3✦ and vengeful, and Mystic Runefish hard-sets every spirit animal's ✦ to 7. What separates this tide from the closely related Grath and Demetrios signatures is its emphasis on hand sculpting and focused threat delivery: Curio Dealer (discard a character to discover one at the same cost) and Shatterpoint Agent (discard to discover upward in cost) appear at 2x alongside Frostbound Defiant, which grants +3✦ to a lone challenger at Night — a single-attacker burst line that rewards deliberate attack sequencing. The Grath and Demetrios tides instead carry Conduit of Resonance and Cindermarch, which mass-trigger Dawn abilities or mass-awaken allies whenever you play a character, making those builds storm harder in a single activation; this tide trades that explosive Dawn-chain ceiling for the ability to search, shape, and concentrate its damage on demand.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
