    {
      "id": "tide-sig-17",
      "name": "Demetrios signature",
      "shortName": "Dawn Chain Swarm",
      "summary": "A spirit animal swarm tide that floods the board with cheap ≤2● characters and converts Dawn triggers into cascading energy, distinguished from its nearest siblings by Conduit of Resonance and Cindermarch as dedicated Dawn-chain amplifiers rather than the void-counting threats or awaken-tempo package those siblings rely on.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-17 is built almost entirely around spirit animals, with over 80% of its cards being Characters and a heavy concentration in the ≤2● cost band. The central engine is the Dawn-trigger economy: cheap spirit animals like Ethereal Trailblazer, Worldsong Behemoth, and Blazebound Sentinel each produce 1● on Dawn, while Skyborne Jellyfish scales that to 1● per allied ≤2● character and Undying Fang can double its yield with three spirit animals in play. Nexus Wayfinder collapses the cost of that whole population to zero, enabling the tide to flood the board and then convert that board into a torrent of energy. The distinctive payoff layer is Conduit of Resonance, which triggers the Dawn ability of every other allied character whenever any character is played, and Cindermarch, which awakens every other allied character upon each materialization — together these turn a single play step into a full-board Dawn chain. Spiritbound Alpha (❖ – 5●: all spirit animals gain +3✦ and vengeful) and Spirit Bond (unstoppable and +X✦ equal to character count) are the late-game finishers that convert the accumulated board and energy into a decisive, often one-turn attack. The closest siblings, Grath (sig-15) and Radulf (sig-16), share the same spirit animal core but orient their top ends differently: sig-15 emphasizes Abomination of Memory and Petal-Seer for a void-counting threat and continuous card access, while sig-16 leans into awaken-tempo with Frostbound Defiant, Mother of Flames, Emberwolf Triad, and Curio Dealer as a sifting and awakening package; sig-17 instead commits to chaining Dawn triggers in bulk through Conduit of Resonance and Cindermarch, making it the most combo-oriented of the three.",
      "role": "signature",
