    {
      "id": "tide-sig-18",
      "name": "Gunnar Deepforge signature",
      "shortName": "Warrior Abandon Ramp",
      "summary": "A warrior flood deck that abandons its own forces to generate energy and upgrade into higher-cost threats, distinguishing itself from its siblings by using sacrifice as a resource engine rather than for spark-transfer or enemy removal.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-18 is built almost entirely out of warriors, with a small complement of fast events, and revolves around treating cheap warriors as fuel rather than finishers. The energy-generation spine is dense: Blood Reaver (2x) turns any warrior abandon into 2●, Wolfbond Chieftain taps to produce 1● per allied warrior, and Frontline Martyr yields 3● on sacrifice, while cost-reduction pieces like Tethered Hollow (2x, first warrior each turn costs 3● less) and Sundown Ronin (2x, all warriors cost 1● less) keep the flood of bodies coming cheaply. That energy feeds the upgrade loop: Spellweaver (2x) cashes out a non-figment warrior for a 1✦ figment, and Aftermath Bloom (2x) requires abandoning a warrior to discover and immediately materialize one with higher cost, escalating the board in steps. Warriors that dissolve or are abandoned return from the void through Burning Revenant (2x), Cinderblade Legionnaire (2x), and Starbound Striker (2x), sustaining the headcount needed for payoffs like Skyflame Commander's support (+1✦ per allied warrior) and Shadow Reflection (fast event, +1✦ per warrior). Where the nearest sibling tide-sig-19 (Tensho) channels abandonment toward enemy dissolution via Eclipse Herald's ⧗-accumulation engine and void recursion through Prism Caller, and tide-sig-20 (Valdren) concentrates its sacrifice on ✦-transfer with Colossal Convergence and on figment generation through Forge-Twin and Crescendo Channeler, tide-sig-18 keeps its sacrifice payoffs squarely in the energy and ladder-upgrade domain, rewarding players who treat each warrior as a coin to spend on the next, larger threat.",
      "role": "signature",
      "cards": [
