    {
      "id": "tide-fac-04",
      "name": "Lean: Nexus Wayfinder",
      "shortName": "Free Swarm Deploy",
      "summary": "A spirit animal flood deck that uses Nexus Wayfinder to make all ≤2● cost characters free, deploying multiple spirits per turn to fuel energy-generating supporters and close with a board-wide spark pump — distinguished from its nearest siblings by centering the cost-reduction engine rather than the mass ✦-equalization finisher those siblings carry.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-04 is built almost entirely around spirit animals, with 35 characters and 10 events, anchored by the Nexus Wayfinder's passive that makes all ≤2● cost characters cost 0● energy. With the majority of the spirit animal roster sitting at 1–2● cost, Nexus Wayfinder converts the deck into a free-deployment machine where multiple spirits flood the board in a single turn. The resulting board presence powers the energy engines: Ghostlight Wolves channels 1● per allied spirit animal and applies a Support +2✦ bonus to whoever it backs; Blazing Emberwing channels 1● per allied character; and Mountainwatch Alpha does the same for the spirit animal subset specifically. Celestial Reverie and Dreamcatcher's Call (both at 2 copies) provide card flow — the former drawing a card each time a character is played, the latter discovering and directly materializing a character at a chosen cost — so the deck can sustain its deploy-and-refill loop without running dry. The ultimate payoff is Spirit Bond (2 copies, 7● cost), which grants all allies unstoppable and +X✦ equal to the number of allied characters, making a wide board of free 1-cost spirits suddenly overwhelming. Compared to sibling tide-fac-13, which runs two copies of Mystic Runefish (setting every spirit animal's ✦ to 7) and two copies of Shatterpoint Agent (discarding cards to discover higher-cost characters), tide-fac-04 invests instead in the cost-reduction engine and the discover-and-materialize toolbox — the play pattern here is about playing everything for free rather than climbing the cost curve or resetting spark values to a fixed ceiling.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"3cda9dd7-cb81-43c1-9db5-1444d7363e13","name":"Spirit Bond","copies":2},
        {"id":"4e3c04a9-1cdd-468a-b42a-40157ed9c9d6","name":"Eternal Stag","copies":2},
        {"id":"965ce3b2-a722-475c-99c5-5b35685d2404","name":"Dreamvale Monarch","copies":2},
