    {
      "id": "tide-fac-05",
      "name": "Lean: Celestial Reverie",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Flood",
      "summary": "A spirit animal swarm that converts board width into energy through Dawn triggers and stored charges, then closes with a board-wide ✦ explosion — distinguished from its nearest siblings by emphasizing energy generation from cheap-creature density rather than drawing or discovering cards.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-05 is a character-heavy (37 of 45 copies) spirit animal swarm built around two interlocking energy engines: Skyborne Jellyfish, which generates 1● at Dawn for each allied character costing 2● or less, and Sunshadow Eagle, which stores 1⧗ each time any spirit animal is materialized and converts three stored charges into 3●. Together these reward the player for flooding the board with low-cost spirit animals quickly, converting board width directly into mana without needing to exhaust a single creature. Support pieces deepen the payoff: Ghostlight Wolves gives supported spirit animals +2✦ while also exhaust-tapping for 1● per spirit animal, Eternal Stag tutors spirit animals from the deck and grants supported ones +1✦, and Mystic Runefish offers a one-shot reset that sets every allied spirit animal's ✦ to 7. The gameplan culminates in Spirit Bond (two copies, 7●), which grants all allies unstoppable and scales each character's ✦ bonus equal to the number of allies present — a lethal alpha-strike that rewards the exact wide board this tide builds. Compared to nearest sibling tide-fac-13, which runs Celestial Reverie and Dreamcatcher's Call at two copies each to chain draw-on-play triggers and free-materialize discoveries, fac-05 replaces those card-selection doubling effects with doubled Skyborne Jellyfish and Sunshadow Eagle, making energy accumulation the primary resource loop rather than card throughput; and compared to tide-fac-22, which leans on cost-specific discover synergies through Lumin-Gate Seer and Curio Dealer, fac-05 keeps its resource generation grounded in body count on the battlefield.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
