    {
      "id": "tide-fac-07",
      "name": "Lean: Dreadcall Warden2",
      "shortName": "Counterspell Outsider Draw",
      "summary": "A tempo-control tide that combines a dense interrupt-speed counterspell suite with an outsider score-draw engine, distinguishing itself from its sibling Driftrider tide by anchoring on reactive card prevention rather than bounce and control-theft.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-07 runs an even split of events and characters (22/23) built around two interlocking engines. The first is a counterspell package dense enough to operate at interrupt speed in most turns: Defiant Parry (×2, Offering — prevent unless opponent pays 1●), Abolish, Ripple Through Reality (prevent and topdeck), Null Sphere, Momentum of the Fallen, Echoing Denial, and characters that double as counterspells — Keeper of the Tides (prevent ≤2● on materialize) and Threadbreaker (Offering body that prevents on materialize). The second engine rewards outsider characters scoring ⍟: Thronebound Arbiter (×2, phasing outsider that draws whenever any allied outsider scores ⍟), Last Beacon (produces 1✦ outsider figments on tap and draws plus gains ⍟ equal to their cost when they score), and Driftrider (foresee 1 and draw on allied outsider score). These two engines combine into a play pattern of holding up counterspells through the opponent's turns while outsider figments and phasing bodies accumulate score triggers that refuel the hand. The Dreadcall Warden2 anchor contributes a ▸Night looting effect that fires every cycle when a challenger is present, tying the low-cost character suite to consistent card filtering. Compared to the nearest sibling tide (tide-fac-06, anchored by Driftrider with Planetgazer), this tide foregoes bounce-and-reuse tools like Annular Recall, Breach Artist's cost-reduction on returned allies, and Cosmic Puppeteer's control-theft, instead doubling down on raw reactive prevention events that deny the opponent's plays outright.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
