    {
      "id": "tide-fac-08",
      "name": "Lean: Sunset Chronicler",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Swarm",
      "summary": "A compact spirit animal flood deck that races to activate Mystic Runefish's mass ✦-equalization ability, converting a board of cheap Dawn-energy producers into unified 7✦ threats — distinct from its sibling signature tides by focusing tightly on that single payoff axis rather than the broader abandon-loop, void-reclaim, and cost-reduction tools those larger pools include.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-08 is an 80% character tide built almost entirely around spirit animals, using a dense cluster of cheap one- and two-cost creatures that generate energy on their Dawn triggers — Undying Fang, Skyborne Jellyfish, Ethereal Trailblazer, Blazebound Sentinel, and several others each produce 1● or more at the start of your turn, collectively funding the tide's central payoff. That payoff is Mystic Runefish (2 copies), whose \"5●, ☪: Each allied spirit animal's ✦ becomes 7\" ability turns a wide board of modest threats into a synchronized alpha strike. A secondary layer of spirit animal lords — Ghostlight Wolves (☪ gains energy per spirit animal; Support +2✦), Lord of Hidden Paths (+1✦ to all spirit animals; draw when you play one), and Eternal Stag (Support +1✦; activated draw) — buffer the board's spark while building toward the Runefish activation, and Spiritbound Alpha provides an emergency combat swing granting all spirit animals +3✦ and vengeful. The tide also carries a figment subtheme through Shardwoven Tyrant (produces figments at Dawn and sacrifices them to dissolve enemies by ✦ count), Embersummoner, and Packcaller of Shadows, giving the deck a removal option that scales with the board state. Sunset Chronicler rounds out the draw package by converting any allied dissolution into a card draw. Compared to the nearest sibling signature tides, which are large comprehensive pools containing the same spirit animal suite alongside abandon-loop machinery (Carrion Lord, Forsaken Pact), cost-reduction infrastructure (Nexus Wayfinder), and void-reclaim tools, this facet strips away all of that secondary architecture and presents a lean, purpose-built package aimed squarely at deploying enough spirit animals to make Mystic Runefish's one-click equalization ability decisive.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
