    {
      "id": "tide-fac-10",
      "name": "Lean: Scorched Reckoning",
      "shortName": "Event Volume Removal",
      "summary": "An event-heavy tide that pairs a high-volume copy engine with a dedicated suite of instant-speed removal, turning the same plays-per-turn count that fuels Hatching Ground's erosion and Call of the Lost's tokens into a reactive threat-answering gameplan that its nearest siblings — the copy-storm fac-03 and the token-generating fac-20 — lack entirely.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-10 is built around an event-volume engine anchored by two copies each of Echo Architect (\"when you play an event, copy it\"), Starcatcher (\"when you play an event, gain 1 energy\"), and Arc Gate Opening (\"gain 4 energy\"), creating a self-fueling loop where each event played generates the resources to play the next. That accumulating play-count then feeds the tide's scalable payoffs: Hatching Ground erodes an enemy X times for each card played this turn, and Call of the Lost materializes one awakened ember figment per card played, both rewarding extended chains. What sets this tide apart from its closest siblings is a dedicated suite of fast and interrupt removal events — Scorched Reckoning dissolves enemies up to 3 spark, Molten Duel handles characters at interrupt speed, Fell the Mighty can reach threats up to 5 spark with an energy premium, Weight of Memory dissolves enemies whose spark is at most the size of your void, and Forsaken Skyline adds a fast dissolve with a built-in reclaim — enabling the pilot to answer threats in the middle of their own chain without interrupting momentum. By contrast, tide-fac-20 (Call of the Lost) channels the same event-copy shell into token generation and void reclaim with two copies of Cascade of Reflections and From the Barrow, and tide-fac-03 (Flash of Power) focuses on raw copy multiplication through double Cascading Detonation and Cascade of Reflections, with neither sibling carrying the reactive removal density that defines this tide's defensive flexibility.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
