    {
      "id": "tide-fac-12",
      "name": "Lean: Infernal Cavalier",
      "shortName": "Dissolved Void Loop",
      "summary": "A warrior-dense tide that uses dissolution triggers to continuously refuel hand and board from the void, distinguished from its closest sibling by centering on automatic dissolved-triggered recursion rather than deliberate abandonment for energy.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-12 is built almost entirely of warriors (42 of 45 copies) and organizes itself around a tight chain of dissolution triggers that keep the hand and board stocked. The anchor engine is Burning Revenant (2 copies): whenever any allied warrior is dissolved, it automatically returns a warrior with lesser cost from the void to hand, creating a self-replenishing loop every time a warrior dies. Multiple other pieces reinforce this directly — Infernal Cavalier and Starbound Striker each trigger on their own dissolution to return another warrior from the void, and Cinderblade Legionnaire does the same while also carrying Vengeful. A mass-resurrection payoff arrives in Wake the Fallen, which materializes all characters that dissolved in the same turn, converting a bad combat step into a sudden board refill. Inferno's Herald adds a second dimension: it accumulates +✦ each dawn and, when dissolved, spawns a wave of 1✦ warrior figments equal to its spark total, rewarding the player for letting it grow before trading it away. Where the closely related sibling tide (Lean: Burning Revenant) pairs its dissolution-return warriors with Blood Reaver as a 2x card — deliberately abandoning warriors to generate energy — this tide treats abandonment as incidental and instead stacks dissolved-trigger recursion pieces so that being attacked and losing warriors becomes a source of card advantage and tempo rather than a cost to pay.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
