    {
      "id": "tide-fac-19",
      "name": "Lean: The Thinning",
      "shortName": "Abandon Disruption",
      "summary": "A sacrifice-and-dissolve engine that pairs abandonment payoffs with targeted hand disruption, distinguishing itself from sibling tides by stacking multiple events that strip specific cards from the opponent's hand alongside fast/interrupt removal.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-19 is a character-heavy facet (32 characters, 13 events) built around abandoning allies to generate energy and score while converting those losses into board and tempo advantages. The abandon engine runs through cards like Nightmare Manifest (abandon a character: gain 1●), Fathomless Maw (abandon a character: gain 1⍟), and Kindlehorn (store ⧗ per abandon, then spend ⧗ to dissolve enemies by spark threshold), converting each sacrifice into a resource or a removal. Dissolution payoffs amplify the loop: Soulreaver draws a card whenever a non-figment ally dissolves, Deathwalker draws on allied survivor deaths, Scuttled Fortune draws for each ally dissolved in a turn, and Duskwall Delver can rematerialize from the void each time any ally dissolves. Where the nearest siblings — the Kell Tarn and Caedryn signature tides — spread the same abandon/dissolve package across a much wider card pool without a consistent secondary angle, this facet carves out a focused hand disruption identity: The Thinning banishes a chosen character from the opponent's hand, Dreaming Groves discards a chosen event from it, and Lurking Dread discards a chosen low-cost card, giving the deck tools to clear threats before they are ever played. A suite of fast/interrupt dissolve events (Burning Pursuit, Pyrokinetic Surge, Ferryman's Tithe, Standoff) rounds out the removal, letting the player answer threats at instant speed in the same turns they are spending allies to fuel the engine. Tide-fac-24 (Stargazer Adrift), the nearest non-signature sibling, runs a much more creature-dense version of the abandonment shell with almost no events, no hand disruption, and no interrupt removal, making it a pure board-presence build rather than the disruptive sacrifice aggro this tide represents.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
