    {
      "id": "tide-fac-24",
      "name": "Lean: Stargazer Adrift",
      "shortName": "Abandon Energy Ramp",
      "summary": "A survivor-dense abandon engine that converts ally dissolution into energy (●) and soul (⍟) gain, culminating in void-recursion loops and a massive reclaim finisher — distinguishing itself from its nearest siblings by emphasizing resource accumulation and late-game payoffs over interrupt-speed removal or card-draw efficiency.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-24 is built almost entirely on characters (41 of 45 copies), with a survivor-tribal core that fuels and rewards deliberate ally dissolution. The central engine runs on three doubled-up payoff characters: Dustborn Veteran replaces every dissolved non-figment survivor with a 1✦ survivor figment, keeping the board populated; Volcanic Channeler generates 1● each time any ally is dissolved, steadily ramping energy; and Silent Avenger gains 1⍟ on each dissolution — a pairing that means every sacrifice yields both ● and ⍟ simultaneously. Kindred Sparks (2x) then feeds back into this by playing itself for just 1● when an allied survivor is already in play, keeping the survivor chain cheap. The generated ⧗ charges and energy curve toward two finishers unique to this tide: Obliterator of Worlds banks one ⧗ per abandon and then spends those charges to execute an enemy by spark threshold, turning accumulated surplus into targeted removal, while The Rising God — an 8-cost, 7✦ Unstoppable character — reclaims for just 2● plus the sacrifice of two characters, giving the tide a decisive endgame. Void-return loops through Graywatch (returns to play when you play any card from your void) and Veil of the Wastes (self-returns from void when a cheap character materializes) support this late arc. Compared to the nearest sibling tide-fac-14, which dedicates event slots to interrupt-speed dissolve effects such as Ferryman's Tithe and Together Against the Tide to cash in on abandons reactively, this tide instead banks those triggers as ● and ⍟ for a slower but more resource-rich payoff; and compared to tide-fac-31, which shares much of the base dissolution economy but supplements it with card-draw (Herald of the Last Light, Burning Pursuit) for board-wide tempo, this tide prioritizes soul and charge accumulation leading to a reclaim-powered apex threat.",
      "role": "facet",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"123baf70-305a-4583-bdba-a10b5153fbeb","name":"Dustborn Veteran","copies":2},
        {"id":"290ea9db-0340-4838-842a-0dea09b5340a","name":"Volcanic Channeler","copies":2},
