    {
      "id": "tide-neu-04",
      "name": "Broad: Blood Reaver / Sigil Analyst",
      "shortName": "Warrior Sacrifice Ramp",
      "summary": "A warrior-dense energy engine that sacrifices cheap warriors via Blood Reaver to fuel accelerated deployment of expensive warriors, distinguished from its siblings by pairing that abandon-to-energy loop with steep cost-reduction and board-wide +✦ scaling rather than dissolved-triggered recursion or figment token generation.",
      "description": "Tide-neu-04 is built almost entirely of warriors (28 of 30 cards are characters, nearly all warrior subtype) and operates around a central abandon-for-energy loop: Blood Reaver (the tide's 2x anchor) converts any warrior into 2● on demand, while Sundown Ronin, Tethered Hollow, Revered Prince, and Dreadmount Sovereign stack cost reductions that let the recovered energy place expensive warriors well ahead of schedule. That energy surplus feeds into a board-wide ✦ payoff layer — Inspiring Templar, Assault Leader, Skyflame Commander, and the fast event Shadow Reflection all scale with the number of allied warriors, so the correct pattern is to sacrifice one or two cheap bodies for fuel and then flood the board to maximize the pump effects. The two upgrade events (Aftermath Bloom and Mirror Protocol) both require abandoning a warrior as their cost and return a discovered warrior of higher cost directly into play, extending the sacrifice loop into a mana-efficient curve-climbing engine. The nearest sibling, tide-fac-17, shares Blood Reaver and some of the warrior shell but centers its identity on dissolved-triggered recursion — Cinderblade Legionnaire and Starbound Striker (each at 2x) return warriors from the void on dissolution, enabling a loop-back gameplan — while also investing heavily in Blade of Unity figment tokens via Forge-Twin and Gilded Catalyst. Tide-fac-29 similarly pairs warrior sacrifice with figment production and sacrifice-for-card-draw outlets (Grim Reclaimer, Blood Moon Ronin). Tide-neu-04 does neither: it has no figment-production payoffs and no dissolved recursion at 2x, instead treating every sacrifice purely as an energy conversion that reduces the cost of the next, bigger warrior and widens the board for a single decisive +✦ burst.",
      "role": "neutral",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"6a3bb4ae-a537-4b79-8bdd-5093f05ec07a","name":"Blood Reaver","copies":2},
        {"id":"1b4d2adc-64ab-4020-bae6-b35321898bf0","name":"Sigil Analyst","copies":1},
        {"id":"1ce0f0f2-4b1a-483d-b93b-74c36e946a08","name":"The Deathsworn","copies":1},
